  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (pca_n2000 + resnet50 + concat, singleprofile) achieved 0.527 acc, while config_043 (scgpt + resnet50 + concat) dropped to 0.427, strongly indicating pca_n2000 is the superior RNA encoder. The only major untested variable in the best config's neighborhood is the image encoder. Question: Does upgrading from resnet50 to the much stronger imagenet_vit_l improve multimodal accuracy? config_047 is an exact single-variable swap from config_001 (only image_encoder changes: resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l; all else identical: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, None aggregation, concat fusion). This clean A/B test isolates the image encoder effect, which is likely the highest-leverage remaining design choice. If it helps, subsequent experiments can stack it with multiprofile/aggregation or weighted fusion; if it doesn't, we rule out that direction and focus on fusion or profile settings. With 7 experiments left, establishing whether the stronger image encoder pays off is the most information-dense next step."
